  "caption": "A complete 128³ DEV volume (NPI-012, S5×30→S3×70) fixed before inference by the largest simulator mobilized-site count among 240 background-free trajectories. The block starts at z=0 of the acquired stack; it contains no rock-exterior background. (a) Initial oil and water. (b,c,e,f) Matched simulator and predicted states at steps 50 and 100. (d) Oil mobilized by step 100, with initial oil support in pale grey. All views share a native-grid orthographic camera, scale and illumination; no smoothing or additional crop is applied. Oil classes are pooled for display and rock is hidden. Predicted surfaces use a fixed 0.5 occupancy threshold. (g) Mobilized fraction from simulator inventories and unthresholded predicted probabilities, reaching 31.53% and 35.44% at step 100. (h) Step-100 mobilization relative to initial oil in each of eight non-overlapping 16-voxel x slabs, using the same unthresholded probabilities. (i) Mean squared occupancy-probability error over initially oil-filled sites, displayed in units of 10^-3. Green solid lines denote the simulator; pink dashed lines denote predictions in (g,h), and the pink line in (i) denotes prediction error. Dotted lines mark the action change after step 30. Curves show this one sample and one frozen seed, not population means or uncertainty. The displacement-selected example is not representative of aggregate performance. Coordinates and simulator steps are not calibrated physical units.",
